 active login path\",\"Created user appworker (uid 1001, shell /bin/ash, locked password) via adduser\",\"Added /etc/security/limits.d/appworker.conf with soft/hard nofile 8192 and soft/hard nproc 256 (standard convention, in case a PAM-aware login path is later enabled)\",\"Added /etc/profile.d/appworker-limits.sh which runs `ulimit -n 8192; ulimit -u 256` scoped to the appworker user, sourced by /etc/profile on every login shell\",\"Found the default system-wide hard nofile cap was 4096, which blocked appworker (unprivileged) from raising nofile to 8192 in a su login-shell test\",\"Fixed the cap by setting rc_ulimit=\\\"-n 8192\\\" in /etc/rc.conf so OpenRC's rc-sysinit raises the default hard nofile ceiling for all subsequently spawned processes at boot\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, sshd active, appworker present, config files in place)\",\"Restarted node1 with the native `reboot` command (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect)\",\"Polled node1 until exec was available again; confirmed boot_id changed, proving a real restart\",\"Post-restart verified sshd active, appworker account intact, config files intact, and that a login shell for appworker now actually achieves ulimit -n 8192 and ulimit -u 256 (previously nofile was capped at 4096)\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"appworker account created on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-989f1053049b4f19\",\"cmd-840cb5d71a034d5a\"],\"summary\":\"adduser created uid=1001(appworker); confirmed present again post-restart via id/getent\"},{\"requirement\":\"login sessions limited to 8192 open files and 256 processes\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a66e8adcd59b418b\",\"cmd-981b448bbf924886\",\"cmd-c558dffecf0342da\",\"cmd-ff2631124a054004\",\"cmd-840cb5d71a034d5a\"],\"summary\":\"limits.d config and profile.d ulimit script created; initial su test showed nofile capped at system default hard=4096 (nproc 256 worked); fixed via rc_ulimit in /etc/rc.conf; post-restart su -l appworker test shows ulimit -n=8192 and ulimit -u=256, proving the login-session limits are actually enforced\"},{\"requirement\":\"pre-restart healthy baseline\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4c19b1c50b064603\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 4e86ee6e-97be-4ae1-a577-a38cb5a89ee8, sshd started, appworker present, config files in place before reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4126df32c51941c4\",\"cmd-030ff914099443ea\",\"cmd-5de77c138d664209\"],\"summary\":\"Backgrounded reboot acknowledged and returned; subsequent exec calls failed (node down); polling succeeded once node1 was back with new boot_id c1393143-ac7c-4c72-940a-784d4bdb8d38, differing from the pre-restart boot_id\"},{\"requirement\":\"post-restart recovery of required services and data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-840cb5d71a034d5a\",\"cmd-d39e09b3ba8148c6\",\"cmd-83e8cb5a8a31447f\"],\"summary\":\"sshd service active again, appworker account and all limit config files intact, and a live login-shell test for appworker confirms nofile=8192 and nproc=256 are functionally enforced after restart\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Created the appworker account on node1 (Alpine 3.23) and gave its login sessions an 8,192 open-file / 256-process limit, verified functional both before and after a full node restart.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1: Alpine Linux, busybox login, no PAM, openssh-server without PAM support — so /etc/security/limits.conf alone would not be enforced by any active login path","Created user appworker (uid 1001, shell /bin/ash, locked password) via adduser","Added /etc/security/limits.d/appworker.conf with soft/hard nofile 8192 and soft/hard nproc 256 (standard convention, in case a PAM-aware login path is later enabled)","Added /etc/profile.d/appworker-limits.sh which runs `ulimit -n 8192; ulimit -u 256` scoped to the appworker user, sourced by /etc/profile on every login shell","Found the default system-wide hard nofile cap was 4096, which blocked appworker (unprivileged) from raising nofile to 8192 in a su login-shell test","Fixed the cap by setting rc_ulimit=\"-n 8192\" in /etc/rc.conf so OpenRC's rc-sysinit raises the default hard nofile ceiling for all subsequently spawned processes at boot","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, sshd active, appworker present, config files in place)","Restarted node1 with the native `reboot` command (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect)","Polled node1 until exec was available again; confirmed boot_id changed, proving a real restart","Post-restart verified sshd active, appworker account intact, config files intact, and that a login shell for appworker now actually achieves ulimit -n 8192 and ulimit -u 256 (previously nofile was capped at 4096)"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"appworker account created on node1","command_ids":["cmd-989f1053049b4f19","cmd-840cb5d71a034d5a"],"summary":"adduser created uid=1001(appworker); confirmed present again post-restart via id/getent"},{"requirement":"login sessions limited to 8192 open files and 256 processes","command_ids":["cmd-a66e8adcd59b418b","cmd-981b448bbf924886","cmd-c558dffecf0342da","cmd-ff2631124a054004","cmd-840cb5d71a034d5a"],"summary":"limits.d config and profile.d ulimit script created; initial su test showed nofile capped at system default hard=4096 (nproc 256 worked); fixed via rc_ulimit in /etc/rc.conf; post-restart su -l appworker test shows ulimit -n=8192 and ulimit -u=256, proving the login-session limits are actually enforced"},{"requirement":"pre-restart healthy baseline","command_ids":["cmd-4c19b1c50b064603"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 4e86ee6e-97be-4ae1-a577-a38cb5a89ee8, sshd started, appworker present, config files in place before reboot"},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-4126df32c51941c4","cmd-030ff914099443ea","cmd-5de77c138d664209"],"summary":"Backgrounded reboot acknowledged and returned; subsequent exec calls failed (node down); polling succeeded once node1 was back with new boot_id c1393143-ac7c-4c72-940a-784d4bdb8d38, differing from the pre-restart boot_id"},{"requirement":"post-restart recovery of required services and data","command_ids":["cmd-840cb5d71a034d5a","cmd-d39e09b3ba8148c6","cmd-83e8cb5a8a31447f"],"summary":"sshd service active again, appworker account and all limit config files intact, and a live login-shell test for appworker confirms nofile=8192 and nproc=256 are functionally enforced after restart"}]},"ttft_ms":1578,"type":"result","duration_ms":186762,"uuid":"92eb7b16-a5af-4638-b592-4ac12b3e7853","ttft_stream_ms":648,"time_to_request_ms":64,"first_content_frame_ms":648,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
